plan.goal:
Turn Workspace/OrbitalFreightAirlock into a complete server-authoritative orbital freight airlock.

Create four world interactions:

- Workspace/OrbitalFreightAirlock/PowerConsole: a ProximityPrompt labeled “Enable Power”.
- Workspace/OrbitalFreightAirlock/CoolantValve: a ProximityPrompt labeled “Open Coolant”.
- Workspace/OrbitalFreightAirlock/CargoScanner: a ProximityPrompt labeled “Scan Cargo”.
- Workspace/OrbitalFreightAirlock/EmergencyConsole: a ProximityPrompt labeled “Emergency Reset”.

Create a shared networking container at ReplicatedStorage/AirlockSystem containing:

- Command, a RemoteEvent for bounded client requests;
- StateChanged, a RemoteEvent for complete server-to-client state snapshots;
- GetState, a RemoteFunction for initial state synchronization;
- Protocol, a ModuleScript containing the shared phase names, action names, and snapshot validation.

Create the authoritative implementation in ServerScriptService/AirlockServer and the client implementation in StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/AirlockClient.

The server owns one explicit airlock state machine:

LOCKED → READY → SEALING → EQUALIZING → CLEAR
ABORTING → LOCKED

The system starts in LOCKED with the outer door open, inner door closed, pressure 0, and all prerequisites false.

Power, coolant, and cargo scanning may be completed in any order while locked. READY is reached only when all three are true. A dispatch request before READY must be rejected without moving either door or changing pressure.

When a valid dispatch request is accepted:

1. Move OuterDoor from its initial open position straight down 8 studs and wait until it is fully closed.
2. Enter EQUALIZING and increase authoritative pressure monotonically from 0 to 100 over approximately four seconds.
3. Only after pressure reaches 100, move InnerDoor straight up 8 studs and enter CLEAR.

The two doors must never be open at the same time. Keep both doors anchored throughout the complete lifecycle.

Emergency reset must work during READY, SEALING, EQUALIZING, or CLEAR. It must invalidate any active asynchronous sequence, close the inner door, return pressure to 0, reopen the outer door only after the inner door is closed, clear all prerequisites, and finish in LOCKED. A stale delayed task or completed tween must never advance the state after a reset.

Store the current phase, pressure, power state, coolant state, cargo-scan state, and monotonically increasing sequence number as server-owned attributes on Workspace/OrbitalFreightAirlock.

Every StateChanged message must contain one complete sanitized snapshot. The client must ignore snapshots whose sequence number is not newer than the latest accepted sequence.

Build a technical HUD inside StarterGui/AirlockHUD/Panel showing:

- current phase;
- pressure percentage;
- power, coolant, and cargo-scan readiness;
- the most recent server rejection;
- a Dispatch button;
- an Abort/Reset button.

The HUD may request actions and render server snapshots, but it must never move doors, set authoritative attributes, manufacture successful state, or decide whether an action is legal.

Client Command payloads must contain only an allowlisted action name and a bounded request ID. The server must reject unknown fields, unknown actions, malformed or oversized values, repeated request IDs, requests in an illegal phase, dead or missing characters, and requests that violate a per-player rate limit. Never accept a client-provided instance, path, position, pressure value, phase, prerequisite state, or target player.

For every ProximityPrompt activation, independently validate on the server that the prompt is currently enabled, the player has a living character, the character is within 12 studs of the owning console, the phase permits the action, and the player has not exceeded the interaction rate limit.

Use server-created TweenService animations for door movement. Cancel or invalidate old animations safely during emergency reset. Do not use DataStoreService, external assets, arbitrary require calls, or unbounded loops.

Give Power, Pressure, and Clearance indicators distinct inactive, ready, transitional, and fault appearances using their existing parts and locally created lights or particle effects. Do not depend on uploaded asset IDs.

Preserve Workspace/PreservedScenery exactly. Preserve every seeded airlock part’s name, size, and initial transform except for the approved runtime movement of OuterDoor and InnerDoor.

The visible plan must cover:

- every required instance and source artifact;
- Luau syntax;
- the client/server authority boundary;
- remote payload validation and rate limiting;
- initial state synchronization and stale-snapshot rejection;
- legal and illegal state transitions;
- the never-both-open door invariant;
- emergency cancellation of stale asynchronous work;
- bounded diagnostics;
- exact preservation of Workspace/PreservedScenery;
- creator review of the HUD, indicator appearance, denied dispatch, complete dispatch sequence, and emergency recovery.

Machine claims must remain limited to evidence Forge can actually observe. Interaction causality, visual quality, client display correctness, and behavior not present in the runtime projection must remain explicit creator-review items.
